# build output
/build/
/build-*/
*.o
*.a

# python worker
worker/.venv/
worker/data/
worker/runs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# research scratch (large corpora, trained tokenizers, sweep outputs)
experiments/*/data/
experiments/*/tokenizers_out/

# local artifacts
*.rnck
*.rnds
*.tmp

# node state — per-machine, and some of it is security-relevant. `addrkey` decides
# this node's address-bucket layout and must stay private or its eclipse
# resistance is gone; `peers.dat` is its own view of the network; the socket is a
# live kernel object and the weights are gigabytes addressed by hash.
addrkey
peers.dat
*.sock
weights/
.rnet/

# editor and OS noise. .vscode/ is NOT ignored: the C++ settings there are what
# make an editor understand C++26 and the src/ include root, and every
# contributor would otherwise rediscover them. Personal overrides go in
# .vscode/settings.local.json, which is.
.vscode/settings.local.json
.vscode/*.log
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
dist/
dist/
build-release/
